{
  "_doc": "Tier-2 pool building (random towns, civic lots): a county library with its reading room two storeys high, the stacks a maze of creaking boards, the librarian's flat over them and the county archive locked in the basement. Route: the front doors are bolted from inside -> round to the back yard, where the fire-escape ladder is down -> up to Ida's back porch and in through the kicked-in kitchen door -> the cage key on its hook in her hall, her diary by her bed -> down the back stair to the workroom -> the stacks: a maze of ranges, every board groans (the stacks' sleepers rise) -> the reading room: they sit at the tables under the tall windows (ambush as you walk in) -> the circulation hall -> the children's corner -> down the cellar stair -> the archive cage: chained, alarmed (loot; the Cordon's clerk guards it) -> back up and out through the bolted front doors. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
